# Template for the root .env (developer credentials for the prep CLI).
#
# Threat model: the devid/devpassword/softname below are a shared,
# non-rotatable, non-scopable client token. They cannot be secured
# client-side — anyone can recover them via a network proxy. The goal is only
# to (a) hide them from casual inspection and (b) keep them out of version
# control and immutable artifacts. This is obfuscation, not security.
#
# The real values are injected at BUILD time from a CI/CD secret (or the
# release engineer's local env). Never commit them. Copy this template to
# .env (git-ignored) and fill in base64-encoded values:
#
#   .venv/bin/python -c \
#     "from es_ost.core.credentials import encode_rc_data; \
#      print(encode_rc_data('DEVID', 'DEVPASSWORD', 'SOFTNAME'), end='')"
#
# Users always supply their own ssid/sspassword in the Refresh dialog.
DEVID=
DEVPASSWORD=
SOFTNAME=
